# What must not go into the build context.
#
# Without this the whole working tree is uploaded to the builder — node_modules alone is
# hundreds of megabytes, and the build then reinstalls it anyway. Worse than slow: a stale
# bin/ or obj/ from a Mac can confuse a Linux restore, and .git carries every secret that
# has ever been committed.

# Node
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.angular/
**/npm-debug.log*

# .NET
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/*.user

# Local state that has no business in an image
**/App_Data/
**/*.env
**/secrets.json
**/appsettings.*.local.json

# Version control and editors
.git/
.gitignore
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
**/.DS_Store

# Docs and scratch — none of it is needed to build or run
docs/
README.md
*.md
!web/README.md
